---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import ResourceLibrary from '../components/ResourceLibrary.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Layout title="Faith & prayers" image="/assets/orthodox-worship.webp"><PageIntro title="The Orthodox faith, lived every day." label="Faith & prayers" description="An introduction to our faith, with prayers and resources together in one place."/>
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <nav class="page-jumps" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#begin">Begin here</a><a href="#prayers">Prayers and resources</a><a href="/homilies/">Listen to homilies</a></nav>
    <section class="intro-two hub-section" id="begin" aria-labelledby="begin-title"><div class="prose"><h2 id="begin-title">Begin with “come and see.”</h2><p>The Orthodox Church preserves the Christian faith handed down by Jesus Christ to His Apostles. Its worship and spiritual life invite us to become more like Christ, one day at a time.</p><p>We pray with hymns and Scripture, with icons and incense. The Divine Liturgy is at the heart of our life together. You are welcome to observe, bring your questions, and learn at your own pace.</p><p>Prayer, the Holy Sacraments, the Scriptures, and acts of love shape this way of life. Father Hans can help you understand what you experience and guide your next steps.</p><a class="button" href="/visit/">Visit us this Sunday <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><figure class="hub-photo"><img src="/assets/orthodox-worship.webp" width="358" height="200" alt="A priest and worshippers holding candles during an Orthodox church service"/><figcaption>Prayer and worship engage the whole person.</figcaption></figure></section>
    <ResourceLibrary/>
  </div>
</Layout>
